          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: હિંમત",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હિંમત — himmat — \"courage\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મારામાં બોલવાની હિંમત નથી. — mārāmā̃ bolvānī himmat nathī — \"I do not have the courage to speak.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હિંમત (himmat) is a loan from Arabic himma, \"resolve, aspiration\", which reached Gujarati through Persian. Its Arabic root is h-m-m, \"to intend\" (Lane)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
